## 1. Scope

This audit covers the agent registry, identity records, lifecycle states, credentials, agent onboarding UI, discovery-to-registration flow, and Python SDK support. It inspects `ophanix-platform/packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/agents`, agent-related migrations, routes in `product_platform/api/app.py`, frontend agent pages, and the standalone `ophanix-python-sdk`. Relevant benchmarks are Microsoft Agent 365 agent registry/quarantine, AWS AgentCore Identity, Google Agent Registry, and enterprise admin visibility patterns. Out of scope: full API key authentication details, which are covered in AUTH.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

The platform has substantial registry scaffolding. `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/db/migrations/0002_agent_registry.up.sql` defines `agents`, `agent_identities`, `agent_capabilities`, `agent_protocols`, `agent_lifecycle_events`, and `agent_heartbeats`. `0003_agent_credentials.up.sql` adds agent credential tables. Domain models live in `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/agents/models.py`; persistence and lifecycle services live in `agents/repository.py`, `agents/identity.py`, `agents/lifecycle.py`, and `agents/credentials.py`.

The API exposes agent registry and credential routes in `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/api/app.py` around the agent registry section near line 9667 and credential routes near line 9862. The Tool Gateway rejects inactive agents in `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/tool_gateway/auth.py:147`, and runtime sessions require active agents in `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/runtime/repository.py:62`. Discovery can create draft registrations around `api/app.py:8401`. The frontend agent UI lives in `packages/product-platform/frontend/src/features/agents/AgentsPage.tsx`, with client calls in `frontend/src/api/agents.ts`. The Python SDK is Tool Gateway focused and the README tells users to register/select active agents externally at `ophanix-python-sdk/README.md:279`.

Current workflow: operators can create drafts, register agents with identity/capability information, view lifecycle data, issue credentials, and see some agent status. The flow is not yet a complete enterprise identity lifecycle with quarantine, revocation, workload identity binding, or end-to-end onboarding from SDK to platform.

