### F-AIR-003 [P0] [Credential Lifecycle] Suspending or decommissioning an agent does not revoke credentials or identities

**Remediation status:** Fixed

**Remediation summary:**
Added lifecycle-driven credential cascade behavior so suspended, restricted, quarantined, revoked, decommissioning, and decommissioned agents revoke active or expiring credentials immediately. Agent identities are marked non-active for restrictive lifecycle states and re-enabled only when allowed lifecycle recovery returns an agent to active. Credential verification now rechecks the latest agent lifecycle and identity status before accepting an otherwise valid token. Tool Gateway token verification now also rejects inactive identities. Lifecycle transitions emit audit events linking lifecycle state changes to credential revocation and revocation publication.

