## 7. Feature-Level Target State

Agent identity should become an enforceable registry, not just metadata. The data model should add enterprise lifecycle states, trust-root-backed workload identity, revocation evidence, credential cascade metadata, and policy bindings. APIs should provide explicit registration, review, activation, quarantine, revocation, rotation, and decommission routes. Services should centralize lifecycle transitions and reuse them across Tool Gateway, runtime sessions, mesh, and plugin governance. UI should support complete onboarding and incident-response workflows. Audit and observability should connect agent identity events to tool calls, sessions, credentials, and trust decisions. Tests should prove that identity state changes have immediate enforcement consequences.
